{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs","id":1171804,"title":"Good names for Packs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-30T09:02:16-08:00","id":1171804,"title":"Good names for Packs","content":"So I need a good name for NPC pack I run - and could not found similar topic for general advises on naming those groups. Any advise or list or generator for naming packs will be looked for - as open question of whole topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The group I look name in particular for is Scandinavian Bone Shadows group that is guarding <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_at_Uppsala\" target=\"_blank\">Temple at Uppsala</a>, for it's lore and sacred place, at the start of Vikings Era in year 800 A.D. For now, I have prepared those pack members:<ul><li><i>Bjarni Death Skull</i> - old Ithaeur and alpha of the pack, one of older priests in Temple.</li> <li><i>Brother Asmund </i>- Wolf-Blooded - middle aged priest in the temple, expert about Norse myths and legends.</li> <li>There are also enigmatic women and men I did not named yet - probably Elodoth and Rahu, respectively. Women, probably, is from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge\">Valkyrie Mot</a> also.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-18-2018, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T11:28:20-08:00","id":1171837,"title":"","content":"General advice? Look toward band names (in this case, metal bands), and change a few things from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T14:04:36-08:00","id":1171888,"title":"","content":"Another suggestion is to look at the names of street gangs as they can serve as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T14:45:50-08:00","id":1171895,"title":"","content":"The Golden Chain seems like an obvious one, given the gold chain wrapped around the place. You could fancify it by calling them the Shackled of Helios or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T15:21:29-08:00","id":1171902,"title":"","content":"You could just call them the Wolves of Uppsala.<br /> Another thought, Odin was served by two ravens and two wolves, maybe name them after one of those wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T20:17:49-08:00","id":1171948,"title":"","content":"The Society of Claws?<br /> <br /> Look up Everchanging Book of Names. It's a random name generator software program.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T01:30:17-08:00","id":1171973,"title":"","content":"Street Stalkers<br /> Totem: the Cat that prowls on the Streets<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Caves<br /> Totem: the Cat that prowls on the Paths<br /> <br /> Its the same pack but their totem upgraded later on the campaign (ate a powerful eagle spirit) as they moved in a more primal territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-31-2017, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T07:54:31-08:00","id":1172257,"title":"","content":"My general approach to something like this is to look at:<br /> \u200b - What is the pack's communal agenda?<br /> \u200b - What does the pack believe?<br /> - What is the pack known for?<br /> - What is the pack's totem?<br /> \u200b - What do regional Uratha politics prioritise?<br /> and then weld together a name symbolically linked to one or more of those.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd look at something straightforward and clearly stating their existence like the Temple Guard, something linked to the shrine like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's suggestion of the Golden Chain (which is probably what I'd end up going with), or something indicating a claim of historical descent and legitimacy like 'Freyr's Children'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:13:35-08:00","id":1172278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172257#post1172257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b - What is the pack's communal agenda?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watching over Temple and secret lore and Fetishes in it, sounds good?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172257#post1172257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b - What does the pack believe?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are Norse Bone Shadows Temple piests - so I think in Spirits and in Norse Gods...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172257#post1172257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b - What is the pack known for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watching over Temple and secret lore and Fetishes in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172257#post1172257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b- What is the pack's totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not have one for time being. As I like to start with Animals for Totems, maybe some variant of Crow or Owl? Choosing Norse Gods patron as Totem is outside of Dark Eras canon for <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> Era...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172257#post1172257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b - What do regional Uratha politics prioritise?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <b>literally</b> the second of three Forsaken packs in nearby of Uppsala. Other two are PCs mix pack of Vikings ( 'Blood for Odin' ) and Hunters in Darkness pack that was just slaughtered by Idigam and it's spawn. So no 'Uratha politics in region', for time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:20:05-08:00","id":1172281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172257#post1172257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'd look at something straightforward and clearly stating their existence like the Temple Guard, something linked to the shrine like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's suggestion of the Golden Chain (which is probably what I'd end up going with), or something indicating a claim of historical descent and legitimacy like 'Freyr's Children'.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Temple Guard' can be too direct - especially, as they are more priests than warriors.<br /> <br /> 'Freyr's Children' would be too limited as Uppsala Temple was sacred for not one, but three Norse gods - Odin, Freyr and Thor, three worshiped at once. So 'Odin's, Freyr's and Thor's Children' maybe to much on the noose and long to prenouncate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And about 'Golden Chain' - What is all about? I cannot recall anything related to Norse myths connected to Gold and Chains at once...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T09:50:03-08:00","id":1172290,"title":"","content":"How about the &quot;Blot Pack&quot;? That's fairly short and would connect you to the main important activity at the temple.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps &quot;Kvasir's Blood&quot;? Seeing as they seem like intellectually talented people..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":".  Touched up the English 01-02-2018, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:11:07-08:00","id":1172297,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ver\u00f0 Viskunnar</span><br /> <br /> It's (probably very bad) Icelandic for &quot;the price of wisdom&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T11:48:27-08:00","id":1172331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172281#post1172281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about 'Golden Chain' - What is all about? I cannot recall anything related to Norse myths connected to Gold and Chains at once...</div> </div> </div> </div>Your wikipedia link mentions the temple being surrounded by a golden chain. ''Adam writes that a golden chain surrounds the temple that hangs from the gables of the building. The chain is very visible to those approaching the temple from a distance due to the landscape where the temple was built; it is surrounded by hills, &quot;like an amphitheatre.&quot;'<br /> <br /> It's even in the picture.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Olaus_Magnus_-_On_the_Glorious_Temple_Devoted_to_the_Nordic_Gods.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T13:56:17-08:00","id":1172374,"title":"","content":"So, Hirfathra Hissu that makes fetishes... That's all there's to the pack in question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T14:06:09-08:00","id":1172381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172331#post1172331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your wikipedia link mentions the temple being surrounded by a golden chain. ''Adam writes that a golden chain surrounds the temple that hangs from the gables of the building. The chain is very visible to those approaching the temple from a distance due to the landscape where the temple was built; it is surrounded by hills, &quot;like an amphitheatre.&quot;'<br /> <br /> It's even in the picture.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Olaus_Magnus_-_On_the_Glorious_Temple_Devoted_to_the_Nordic_Gods.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Golden Chain too. If you want some mythological resonance for it, Wyrd, there's some space to work with the golden necklace Brisingamen, which belonged to Freyja. Considering she and Frey were brother and sister, loved each other and, she was at the same time a goddess of love, fertility and war, I think there are worse examples of heritage for a pack in this context.<br /> <br /> (Frejya is cool)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T16:06:04-08:00","id":1173103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172381#post1172381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Frejya is cool)</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. When I was a kid I named my pet rabbit after her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T20:32:29-08:00","id":1173151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1172381#post1172381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with Golden Chain too. If you want some mythological resonance for it, Wyrd, there's some space to work with the golden necklace Brisingamen, which belonged to Freyja. Considering she and Frey were brother and sister, loved each other and, she was at the same time a goddess of love, fertility and war, I think there are worse examples of heritage for a pack in this context.<br /> <br /> (Frejya is cool)</div> </div> </div> </div>And death! And magic!<br /> She and her brother stopped sleeping with each other after the alliance with the Aesir though, as they disapprove of sibling-relationships like that.<br /> <br /> But yes. Freyja is insanely cool.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/XLjjS23.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T02:56:34-08:00","id":1173188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1173151#post1173151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( Goddess of Love, Fertility and War... ) And death! And magic!<br /> She and her brother stopped sleeping with each other after the alliance with the Aesir though, as they disapprove of sibling-relationships like that.<br /> <br /> But yes. Freyja is insanely cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will go with <i>Golden Chain</i> for Uppsala Temple pack name. But when need to use some Bone Shadows and Storm Lords pack - for example for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1065711-2e-fan-valkyrie-mot-as-lodge\">Valkyrie Mot Lodge</a> - I will use <i>Daughters of Freyja</i> as pack name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ( Freyja still got good relations with Odin and valkyries, yes? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T04:17:10-08:00","id":1173193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1173151#post1173151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And death! And magic!<br /> She and her brother stopped sleeping with each other after the alliance with the Aesir though, as they disapprove of sibling-relationships like that.<br /> <br /> But yes. Freyja is insanely cool.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Vanir thing. I actually intended &quot;love&quot; in a non-Lannister sense, since all the versions I read of the Norse myths pointed out the two cared a lot for each other (even when Freyr falls in love with Gerdr), but it's worth mentioning that as well.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, gotta love those female characters so badass that all Asgard is afraid to make them angry. Freyja is probably my favorite, but I also like Skadi and Hela for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1173188#post1173188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ( Freyja still got good relations with Odin and valkyries, yes? )</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, depends. Freyja gets half of the worthy souls of those who die in battle, while the other goes to Odin in the Valhalla, She's also connected to the valkyries, as a choser of the slain, though they serve Odin (I read once Odin lends some to Frejya as attendants, but that was ages ago and can't recall the source). Some modern interpretations give Odin the valkyries and Freyja the disir, but that's basically modern people connecting the dots (which is cool and something I do as well when I write mythology fiction, but not supported by much real informations) Depending on the version you're reading, Freyja is either cool with that or mildy annoyed by Odin and the valkyrie's having rights over those who die a warrior's death.<br /> <br /> I tend to look at it as if she made peace with the fact, because Odin's the king and everyone knows he's also a fucking magpie when it comes to purviews, powers and that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I'd say that, in a Forsaken context, you can run with that name and not have any issue with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-04-2018, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T22:25:08-07:00","id":1345169,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting topic, as I prepare much larger, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1344875-dark-eras-fan-constantinople-%E2%80%93-early-medieval-istanbul-turkey-%E2%80%93-700-%E2%80%93-1000-ad\">Constantinopole setting</a> in year 800 AD. I need a name for this pack concept - <b><i>Bone Shadows watching over Imperial Library of Constantinopole</i></b>, with help from mages in Keepers of the Word Order. / One of two prequel Orders to Mysterium./ ( As Omphalos / Rosseta Society faction in city. )<br /> <br /> I <i>already</i> have Hunter in Darkness pack watching over Hagia Sophia, around it and under it ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basilica_Cistern\" target=\"_blank\">Basilica Cistern</a> ) that I think I name <b><i>H</i><i>ounds of God</i></b> - as they HiD are also part of Jeremiad Sworn faction in city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2019, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T22:59:14-07:00","id":1345171,"title":"","content":"Grab some appropriate terms. Curators. Cenobite. Sage. Scribe, Scripture. Then tie them to something else, either related to what they do, how they do it, or what they do it from. You can go with a simple, 'the Curators' or 'The Curators of the Seven Scriptures,' since Constantine was big on transcribing the religious works there might be a few things they made sure never made it to mortal eyes but allow for study and maybe can offer some wisdom in time of need. Or perhaps they protected the works that weren't officially transcribed, and they are the Bearers of the Lost Truths, waiting for some folks to ask the right questions. You get the idea, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T23:32:21-07:00","id":1345173,"title":"","content":"'Ceno-bites' ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) are interesting name for werewolves pack. 'Cenobites of Lost Truths' sounds as interesting mix and point's they always look for forgotten text in Library, that is often described as 'losing' many of it's scriptures inside it's vast halls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T04:20:23-07:00","id":1345193,"title":"","content":"Next pack name needed...<br /> <br /> <b>Uratha Pack - <i>??? </i>( ??? )</b><br /> <br /> Blood Talons and Storm Lords werewolves inside Emperor\u2019s guard unit in Great Palace \u2013 palace complex that is city into itself. ??? are looking over well-being of the Roman Eagle that is Patron of Empire in Shadow Realm, hovering over Great Palace as Spirit Lord. They are &quot;eagle-bearers&quot; (gr. Ornith\u00f3voras), descendants of the aquilifers of the Roman legions that started Eastern Empire centuries before. ??? are known to support <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1166388#post1166388\">Themisine Protectorate of Pure</a>, \u2018for the good of Empire\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ideas like 'Emperor's Finest' or 'Children of Eagle' sounds to simply, don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T13:17:49-07:00","id":1345315,"title":"","content":"Hoplites of Urfarah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T13:46:53-07:00","id":1345320,"title":"","content":"Can always use the name of an NPC for them, the Scions of Lycurgis. But in this case you have an easy go-to with the Eagle. If they view themselves as an extension of the eagle you can call them Talons, or Wings. If they view themselves as subservient like they're a lodge they can be something like 'Old Eagle's Shadow,' or 'Bolts of the Eagle' just because if I recall correctly the ones from Rome had some lightning theme going with them. Second edition usually promotes the idea of totems as equals, so they might consider themselves the 'Convocation of Eagles' where they are all eagles (convocation is a plurality of eagles). But due to their position as the Emperor's guard and being in the palace they might be a Court of Eagles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T23:51:28-07:00","id":1345538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171804-good-names-for-packs?p=1345320#post1345320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...they might consider themselves the 'Convocation of Eagles' where they are all eagles (convocation is a plurality of eagles). But due to their position as the Emperor's guard and being in the palace they might be a Court of Eagles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lighting Eagle was Roman symbol. Byzantine one was Eagle on the Staff, without Lighting. I have a small problem with calling Blood Talons wolves as 'Court' - they are not so 'dyplomatic' for that, going always for duels. I went with 'Assembly of Eagles' name for this pack - in greek: <i>Syn\u00e9lefsi ton Aet\u00f3n. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T00:35:39-07:00","id":1345543,"title":"","content":"Two new packs ideas I have, that needs names for them...<br /> <br /> <b><i>??? </i> ( ??? )</b><br /> <br /> Pack of Hunters in Darkness and Iron Masters werewolves, looking over various markets and trade in Constantinople from exotic threats for it \u2013 like Hosts in bales of silk ( threat of Azlu spiders ) or in grains storages ( threat of Beshilu rats ) \u2013 or humans trafficking with things they should no. / Important fact \u2013 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Bazaar,_Istanbul\" target=\"_blank\">Grand Bazaar</a> as we know is from Turkish times, started in 1456 AD. Before that all Byzantine markets were open under sky. /<br /> <br /> <b><i>??? </i> ( ??? )</b><br /> <br /> Pack of Blood Talons and Iron Masters werewolves, looking over chariots <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nika_riots#Background\" target=\"_blank\">demes</a> \u2013 medieval sport-political \u2018clubs\u2019 for charioteers teams, that were much importance in day-to-day life of lower rungs of Empire\u2019s society. After famous <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nika_riots#Riots\" target=\"_blank\">Nika Riots</a> in 532 AD that destroyed almost half of Constantinopole and previous cathedral \u2013 Forsaken understood they need to look over \u2018demes rioters\u2019, to judge they dangers to people, especially from threats of Shadow and Uratha in their midst. Members are often infiltrate demes teams, literally changing colors \u2013 and skins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}